/**

@page applications_exahype2_exaskred ExaSkred

\tableofcontents

ExaSkred takes its name from the Norwegian word `jordskred`:
https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jordskred

ExaSkred is the collective name for the hazard applications of ExaHyPE.

The current ExaSkred sub-applications are:

\li `coupled`
\li `tsunami`
\li `landslide`
\li `meteotsunami`

Each application directory contains the code it needs to build and run its own
set of cases: setup scripts, kernels, source terms, runtime parameters, and
scenario data. Some components are shared where the same solver logic is used
in more than one place, but the application-specific parts stay local to the
respective subdirectory.

# Scope

`tsunami` collects tsunami scenarios driven by prescribed initial disturbances
or benchmark-style setups.

`meteotsunami` covers atmospherically forced long-wave events and augments the
hydrodynamic core with pressure, friction, rotation, and projection utilities.

`landslide` contains slide-generated wave applications with their own
topography, forcing, and admissibility logic.

`coupled` focuses on coupled landslide-tsunami experiments where slide motion
and wave propagation interact.

*/
